    "created_at": "2018-02-17T19:45:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-17T19:45:04Z",
    "body": "Thanks for getting this started. The changes you've made so far make sense to me but per [my comment in #3468](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3468#issuecomment-365656022), I personally think it would make better logical sense for the reset algorithm to set the text entry cursor to the beginning of the text control, remove any selection, and set the selection direction to \"none\". When the reset algorithm is invoked, the user wants to return the control to its initial state, so IMO it doesn't make sense to retain the existing cursor / selection bounds (which might even relate to a different pre-reset value).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
